From 1b4c37adddc5a5bedb7f2e630fe39727c90fceca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:45:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cli): camcraft-cli --ui sends MCP tool calls to the
 running window

Each CamCraft window opens a UI link at start: a Unix domain socket on
Unix, a 127.0.0.1-only TCP port on Windows (std has no named pipe; the
dependency question is on #3751). A discovery file <pid>.json in the
user's link folder names it, with a random token that each connection
must send first. `camcraft-cli --ui call <tool> [<json>]`, `--ui mcp`
and `--ui windows` find a window (by --window <pid|project> when
several run) and send MCP JSON-RPC, which the window answers in
mcp_host::pump on its own History, so Ctrl+Z undoes a CLI step. With
no window the lane exits 3 and runs nothing; it never falls back to a
headless document.

Refs #3751

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
